From 9f7fe2a89457a9799e3cc6c0ddfb437468798947 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77ph <tk@itarragon.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:20:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] feat(operator): `jinn signer-migrate` -- one-step
 handover to the Kernel owner

Moves a bootstrapped operator to its hardware-signed Kernel account
(config.signer) in one idempotent command; every step reads the chain first
and is skipped when already done.

  1. kernel-approves-safe  the Kernel signs IdentityRegistry
                           setApprovalForAll(Safe, true) via agent-signer --
                           deploying itself if needed and proving the
                           hardware key can sign before it receives anything
  2. mandate-admits-safe   its AgentPolicy must admit (Safe, execTransaction)
  3. safe-owner            the agent EOA swaps itself out for the Kernel
  4. agent-nft             the agent EOA transfers the ERC-8004 NFT
  5. attestation-key       the Kernel publishes the EOA as jinn.attestationKey
  6. eoa-has-no-authority  final check

The service Safe and, when separate, the fleet identity Safe are migrated.
--dry-run prints the plan from the chain; --yes confirms.

- src/signer/migrate.ts (migrateToKernelOwner), src/cli/commands/
  signer-migrate.ts, registered in src/cli/index.ts.
- tests: unit (no handover to a Kernel whose mandate does not admit the Safe
  or that is not deployed -- mutation-checked; 1/1 Safes only; a dry run
  sends nothing); the Kernel-owner hermetic loop now migrates with it --
  dry run, run, idempotent re-run -- before the daemon's solution loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
